  "notes": "A mirrored pair; one half transcribed. Gothic: castellated parapet with corner turrets, pointed windows, gabled dormers, cresting along the ridge. 'Two semi-detached Villas, which may, however, with a little modification be erected continuously.' The specification gives the library as 14 by 12 and the plate as 14 by 13; the plate's is recorded. The attic has a prospect room of six feet six by six, and eight closets, and 'the Roof slopes into these Rooms, and they are lighted by Dormer Windows'. 3000 pounds the pair. The bed room and attic floors are dimensioned on page 167, at a stated scale of twelve feet to one inch, and they agree with the specification room for room. The bath room and the dressing room are both six feet square, which is what a bath room was.",
